    "text": "A proton, an electron, and a Helium nucleus, have the same energy. They are in circular orbits in a plane due to magnetic field perpendicular to the plane. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></msub></math> be their respective radii, then,",
